Usage : EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange""" .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#EquivalentBranch.positiveX21
cim:EquivalentBranch.positiveX21 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                 rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch ;
                                 rdfs:range cim:Reactance ;
                                 rdfs:comment """Positive sequence series reactance from terminal sequence 2 to terminal sequence 1. Used for short circuit data exchange according to IEC 60909
Usage : EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange""" .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#EquivalentBranch.r
cim:EquivalentBranch.r rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                       rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch ;
                       rdfs:range cim:Resistance ;
                       rdfs:comment "Positive sequence series resistance of the reduced branch." .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#EquivalentBranch.r21
cim:EquivalentBranch.r21 rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                         rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch ;
                         rdfs:range cim:Resistance ;
                         rdfs:comment """Resistance from terminal sequence 2 to terminal sequence 1 .Used for steady state power flow. This attribute is optional and represent unbalanced network such as off-nominal phase shifter. If only EquivalentBranch.r is given, then EquivalentBranch.r21 is assumed equal to EquivalentBranch.r.
Usage rule : EquivalentBranch is a result of network reduction prior to the data exchange.""" .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#EquivalentBranch.x
cim:EquivalentBranch.x rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                       rdfs:domain cim:EquivalentBranch ;
