###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#PanDemandResponse.heatingOffset
cim:PanDemandResponse.heatingOffset rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                    rdfs:domain cim:PanDemandResponse ;
                                    rdfs:range cim:Temperature ;
                                    rdfs:comment "Requested offset to apply to the normal heating setpoint at the time of the start of the event. It represents a temperature change that will be applied to the associated heating set point. The temperature offsets will be calculated per the local temperature in the thermostat. The calculated temperature will be interpreted as the number of degrees to be subtracted from the heating set point. Sequential demand response events are not cumulative. The offset shall be applied to the normal setpoint." .


