The attribute shall have a positive value.""" .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RotatingMachine.ratedU
cim:RotatingMachine.ratedU rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                           rdfs:domain cim:RotatingMachine ;
                           rdfs:range cim:Voltage ;
                           rdfs:comment "Rated voltage (nameplate data, Ur in IEC 60909-0). It is primarily used for short circuit data exchange according to IEC 60909." .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RotatingMachineDynamics.inertia
cim:RotatingMachineDynamics.inertia rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                    rdfs:domain cim:RotatingMachineDynamics ;
                                    rdfs:range cim:Seconds ;
                                    rdfs:comment "Inertia constant of generator or motor and mechanical load (H) (&gt;0).  This is the specification for the stored energy in the rotating mass when operating at rated speed.  For a generator, this includes the generator plus all other elements (turbine, exciter) on the same shaft and has units of MW*sec.  For a motor, it includes the motor plus its mechanical load. Conventional units are per unit on the generator MVA base, usually expressed as MW*second/MVA or just second.   This value is used in the accelerating power reference frame for operator training simulator solutions.  Typical Value = 3." .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RotatingMachineDynamics.statorLeakageReactance
cim:RotatingMachineDynamics.statorLeakageReactance rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                   rdfs:domain cim:RotatingMachineDynamics ;
