###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Sectionaliser
cim:Sectionaliser rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf cim:Switch ;
                  rdfs:comment "Automatic switch that will lock open to isolate a faulted section. It may, or may not, have load breaking capability. Its primary purpose is to provide fault sectionalising at locations where the fault current is either too high, or too low, for proper coordination of fuses." .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SecurityConstraintSum
cim:SecurityConstraintSum rdf:type owl:Class ;
                          rdfs:subClassOf cim:MarketFactors ;
                          rdfs:comment """Typically provided by RTO systems, constraints identified in both base case and critical contingency cases have to be transferred.
A constraint has N (&gt;=1) constraint terms. A term is represented by an
instance of TerminalConstraintTerm. 
The constraint expression is:
minValue &lt;= c1*x1 + c2*x2 + .... cn*xn + k &lt;= maxValue
where:
- cn is ConstraintTerm.factor 
- xn is the flow at the terminal
Flow into the associated equipment is positive for the purpose of ConnectivityNode NodeConstraintTerm

k is SecurityConstraintsLinear.resourceMW
The units of k are assumed to be same as the units of the flows, xn.  The constants, cn, are dimensionless.
With these conventions, cn and k are all positive for a typical constraint such as \"weighted sum of generation shall be less than limit\". Furthermore, cn are all 1.0 for a case such as \"interface flow shall be less than limit\", assuming the terminals are chosen on the importing side of the interface.""" .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SecurityConstraints
cim:SecurityConstraints rdf:type owl:Class ;
                        owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                              owl:onProperty cim:SecurityConstraints.actualMW ;
                                              owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                              owl:onClass cim:ActivePower
                                            ] ,
                                            [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                              owl:onProperty cim:SecurityConstraints.maxMW ;
                                              owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                              owl:onClass cim:ActivePower
                                            ] ,
                                            [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                              owl:onProperty cim:SecurityConstraints.minMW ;
                                              owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                              owl:onClass cim:ActivePower
                                            ] ;
                        rdfs:subClassOf cim:IdentifiedObject ;
                        rdfs:comment "Typical for regional transmission operators (RTOs), these constraints include transmission as well as generation group constraints identified in both base case and critical contingency cases." .


###  http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#SecurityConstraintsClearing
cim:SecurityConstraintsClearing rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                owl:equivalentClass [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                      owl:onProperty cim:SecurityConstraintsClearing.mwFlow ;
                                                      owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                      owl:onClass cim:ActivePower
                                                    ] ,
                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                      owl:onProperty cim:SecurityConstraintsClearing.mwLimit ;
                                                      owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                      owl:onClass cim:ActivePower
                                                    ] ,
                                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                                      owl:onProperty cim:SecurityConstraintsClearing.shadowPrice ;
                                                      owl:maxQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                                                      owl:onClass cim:Money
                                                    ] ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf cim:MarketFactors ;
                                rdfs:comment "Binding security constrained clearing results posted for a given settlement period." .


